{"text": "MAYOR, POLICE HUDDLE; MAP 'B-DAY' TACTICS\n\nTHOMAS FITZPATRICK\n\nChicago Tribune (1963-Current file);\n\nSep 4, 1964;\n\nProQuest Historical Newspapers Chicago Tribune (1849 - 1987)\n\npg. 10\n\nMAYOR, POLICE\nHUDDLE; MAP\nB-DAYTACTICS\n\nBeatles\u2019 Arrival Being\nKept Secret\n\nBY THOMAS FITZPATRICK\nThe in Mayor Da-\n\nl\u00e9y\u2019s office ended abruptly\n\nyesterday . and .,.\nfive grim-faced \u00abi\nmen: strode\n\nswiftly out the\nars \u201cRobert\n\nforce,\nand gave the\nmayor. one\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry, Mr. Mayor,\u201d\nhe said. \u201cWe've been in tight\nspots before. We'll handle the\n\nlice, fire, traffic, \u2018and health\n\n| departments.\n\n\u201cWe hope we've covered all\n\nm= the bases. We know they've\n\ncaused trouble everywhere else\nthey\u2019ve been but we think we're\nprepared for anything.\u201d\nThe Beatles will appear in\nMilwaukee tonight and s0 it\nwasn\u2019t certain whether they\nwould fly into Chicago or drive.\n\n* Reilly declined to elaborate on\n\nthe plans of the four.\n\u201cOur _plan is simple,\u201d he\nsaid. \u201cWe're going to try to\nsneak them in and sneak them\n\nBeatl\u00e9s just like every oth\u00e9r out.\u201d\n\nbig emergency. .JIt calls for\nHight security and a stiff upper\nDp\u201d :\nMayor Daley nodded but did\nnot smile.\nJack Reilly, the mayor's di-\nrector \u2018of special events, a\nhuge bundle of newspaper clip-\npings in his hand, walked un-\nsmiling toward a little knot of\nreporters.\n\u201cBeatles Are Coming\u201d\n\u201cGentlemen,\u201d he began, \u201cas\nyou all know the Beatles will\nbe in Chicago tomorrow. We\nhave just held a meeting with\nthe mayor that was attended\nby representatives of the po-\n\n\u201cLt. Lynskey stepped forward.\n\u2018Not Room for All\n\u201cThere is only one difficulty\nwith that plan,\u201d he said. \u201c\u2018Soon-\ner or later they're going to\nhave to show up at the Amphi-\ntheater. Our information is that\n13,260 seats have been sold.\nThere are no more to sell but\nthere are thousands more Bea-\ntle fans who will try to get\nin\u201d\n\nLynskey said 300 patrolmen\nwill be in the vicinity of 43d\nand Halsted streets to handle\nthe crowds. -\n\u201cIf they get to be too big,\u201d\nhe said, \u2018we'll just close off\n\nHalsted street for a couple of\nblocks\u2019 and let them walk in\nthe streets.\u201d\nLynskey shook hands with\nReilly and Fire Commissioner\nRobert J. Quinn: Stil] no smiles.\n\u201cGood luck to-you both,\u201d said\nQuinn. \u201cI hope we all get thru\nthis thing unscathed.\u201d\n\nReproduced with permission of the copyright owner. Further reproduction prohibited without permission.",
